{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This guide covers patterns for controlling where code runs in your TanStack Start application - server-only, client-only, or isomorphic (both environments). For foundational concepts, see the "},{"type":"link","href":"./execution-model.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Execution Model"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set up execution boundaries in your TanStack Start application:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createServerFn,\n  createServerOnlyFn,\n  createClientOnlyFn,\n  createIsomorphicFn,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\n// Server function (RPC call)\nconst getUsers = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  return await db.users.findMany()\n})\n\n// Server-only utility (crashes on client)\nconst getSecret = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.API_SECRET)\n\n// Client-only utility (crashes on server)\nconst saveToStorage = createClientOnlyFn((data: any) => {\n  localStorage.setItem('data', JSON.stringify(data))\n})\n\n// Different implementations per environment\nconst logger = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server((msg) => console.log(`[SERVER]: ${msg}`))\n  .client((msg) => console.log(`[CLIENT]: ${msg}`))","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"implementation-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Implementation Patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"progressive-enhancement","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Progressive Enhancement"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Component works without JS, enhanced with JS\nfunction SearchForm() {\n  const [query, setQuery] = createSignal('')\n\n  return (\n    <form action=\"/search\" method=\"get\">\n      <input\n        name=\"q\"\n        value={query()}\n        onChange={(e) => setQuery(e.target.value)}\n      />\n      <ClientOnly fallback={<button type=\"submit\">Search</button>}>\n        <SearchButton onSearch={() => search(query())} />\n      </ClientOnly>\n    </form>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"environment-aware-storage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment-Aware Storage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const storage = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server((key: string) => {\n    // Server: File-based cache\n    const fs = require('node:fs')\n    return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('.cache', 'utf-8'))[key]\n  })\n  .client((key: string) => {\n    // Client: localStorage\n    return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key) || 'null')\n  })","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-problems","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Problems"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"environment-variable-exposure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variable Exposure"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Exposes to client bundle\nconst apiKey = process.env.SECRET_KEY\n\n// ✅ Server-only access\nconst apiKey = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.SECRET_KEY)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"incorrect-loader-assumptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Incorrect Loader Assumptions"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Assuming loader is server-only\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users')({\n  loader: () => {\n    // This runs on BOTH server and client!\n    const secret = process.env.SECRET // Exposed to client\n    return fetch(`/api/users?key=${secret}`)\n  },\n})\n\n// ✅ Use server function for server-only operations\nconst getUsersSecurely = createServerFn().handler(() => {\n  const secret = process.env.SECRET // Server-only\n  return fetch(`/api/users?key=${secret}`)\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users')({\n  loader: () => getUsersSecurely(), // Isomorphic call to server function\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hydration-mismatches","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydration Mismatches"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Different content server vs client\nfunction CurrentTime() {\n  return <div>{new Date().toLocaleString()}</div>\n}\n\n// ✅ Consistent rendering\nfunction CurrentTime() {\n  const [time, setTime] = createSignal<string>()\n\n  createEffect(() => {\n    setTime(new Date().toLocaleString())\n  })\n\n  return <div>{time() || 'Loading...'}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"production-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production Checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bundle Analysis"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Verify server-only code isn't in client bundle"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Ensure secrets use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createServerOnlyFn()"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createServerFn()"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Loader Logic"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Remember loaders are isomorphic, not server-only"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ClientOnly Fallbacks"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Provide appropriate fallbacks to prevent layout shift"}]}],"checked":false},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Boundaries"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Handle server/client execution errors gracefully"}]}],"checked":false}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related-resources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related Resources"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./execution-model.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Execution Model"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Core concepts and architectural patterns"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./server-functions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Functions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Deep dive into server function patterns"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./environment-variables.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Secure environment variable handling"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./middleware.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Server function middleware patterns"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"quick-start","text":"Quick Start","level":2},{"id":"implementation-patterns","text":"Implementation Patterns","level":2},{"id":"progressive-enhancement","text":"Progressive Enhancement","level":3},{"id":"environment-aware-storage","text":"Environment-Aware Storage","level":3},{"id":"common-problems","text":"Common Problems","level":2},{"id":"environment-variable-exposure","text":"Environment Variable Exposure","level":3},{"id":"incorrect-loader-assumptions","text":"Incorrect Loader Assumptions","level":3},{"id":"hydration-mismatches","text":"Hydration Mismatches","level":3},{"id":"production-checklist","text":"Production Checklist","level":2},{"id":"related-resources","text":"Related Resources","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis guide covers patterns for controlling where code runs in your TanStack Start application - server-only, client-only, or isomorphic (both environments). For foundational concepts, see the [Execution Model](./execution-model.md) guide.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nSet up execution boundaries in your TanStack Start application:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createServerFn,\n  createServerOnlyFn,\n  createClientOnlyFn,\n  createIsomorphicFn,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\n// Server function (RPC call)\nconst getUsers = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  return await db.users.findMany()\n})\n\n// Server-only utility (crashes on client)\nconst getSecret = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.API_SECRET)\n\n// Client-only utility (crashes on server)\nconst saveToStorage = createClientOnlyFn((data: any) => {\n  localStorage.setItem('data', JSON.stringify(data))\n})\n\n// Different implementations per environment\nconst logger = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server((msg) => console.log(`[SERVER]: ${msg}`))\n  .client((msg) => console.log(`[CLIENT]: ${msg}`))\n```\n\n## Implementation Patterns\n\n### Progressive Enhancement\n\n```tsx\n// Component works without JS, enhanced with JS\nfunction SearchForm() {\n  const [query, setQuery] = createSignal('')\n\n  return (\n    <form action=\"/search\" method=\"get\">\n      <input\n        name=\"q\"\n        value={query()}\n        onChange={(e) => setQuery(e.target.value)}\n      />\n      <ClientOnly fallback={<button type=\"submit\">Search</button>}>\n        <SearchButton onSearch={() => search(query())} />\n      </ClientOnly>\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Environment-Aware Storage\n\n```tsx\nconst storage = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server((key: string) => {\n    // Server: File-based cache\n    const fs = require('node:fs')\n    return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('.cache', 'utf-8'))[key]\n  })\n  .client((key: string) => {\n    // Client: localStorage\n    return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key) || 'null')\n  })\n```\n\n## Common Problems\n\n### Environment Variable Exposure\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Exposes to client bundle\nconst apiKey = process.env.SECRET_KEY\n\n// ✅ Server-only access\nconst apiKey = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.SECRET_KEY)\n```\n\n### Incorrect Loader Assumptions\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Assuming loader is server-only\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users')({\n  loader: () => {\n    // This runs on BOTH server and client!\n    const secret = process.env.SECRET // Exposed to client\n    return fetch(`/api/users?key=${secret}`)\n  },\n})\n\n// ✅ Use server function for server-only operations\nconst getUsersSecurely = createServerFn().handler(() => {\n  const secret = process.env.SECRET // Server-only\n  return fetch(`/api/users?key=${secret}`)\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users')({\n  loader: () => getUsersSecurely(), // Isomorphic call to server function\n})\n```\n\n### Hydration Mismatches\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Different content server vs client\nfunction CurrentTime() {\n  return <div>{new Date().toLocaleString()}</div>\n}\n\n// ✅ Consistent rendering\nfunction CurrentTime() {\n  const [time, setTime] = createSignal<string>()\n\n  createEffect(() => {\n    setTime(new Date().toLocaleString())\n  })\n\n  return <div>{time() || 'Loading...'}</div>\n}\n```\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- [ ] **Bundle Analysis**: Verify server-only code isn't in client bundle\n- [ ] **Environment Variables**: Ensure secrets use `createServerOnlyFn()` or `createServerFn()`\n- [ ] **Loader Logic**: Remember loaders are isomorphic, not server-only\n- [ ] **ClientOnly Fallbacks**: Provide appropriate fallbacks to prevent layout shift\n- [ ] **Error Boundaries**: Handle server/client execution errors gracefully\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- [Execution Model](./execution-model.md) - Core concepts and architectural patterns\n- [Server Functions](./server-functions.md) - Deep dive into server function patterns\n- [Environment Variables](./environment-variables.md) - Secure environment variable handling\n- [Middleware](./middleware.md) - Server function middleware patterns\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: code-execution-patterns\ntitle: Code Execution Patterns\n---\n\nThis guide covers patterns for controlling where code runs in your TanStack Start application - server-only, client-only, or isomorphic (both environments). For foundational concepts, see the [Execution Model](./execution-model.md) guide.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nSet up execution boundaries in your TanStack Start application:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createServerFn,\n  createServerOnlyFn,\n  createClientOnlyFn,\n  createIsomorphicFn,\n} from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\n// Server function (RPC call)\nconst getUsers = createServerFn().handler(async () => {\n  return await db.users.findMany()\n})\n\n// Server-only utility (crashes on client)\nconst getSecret = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.API_SECRET)\n\n// Client-only utility (crashes on server)\nconst saveToStorage = createClientOnlyFn((data: any) => {\n  localStorage.setItem('data', JSON.stringify(data))\n})\n\n// Different implementations per environment\nconst logger = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server((msg) => console.log(`[SERVER]: ${msg}`))\n  .client((msg) => console.log(`[CLIENT]: ${msg}`))\n```\n\n## Implementation Patterns\n\n### Progressive Enhancement\n\n```tsx\n// Component works without JS, enhanced with JS\nfunction SearchForm() {\n  const [query, setQuery] = createSignal('')\n\n  return (\n    <form action=\"/search\" method=\"get\">\n      <input\n        name=\"q\"\n        value={query()}\n        onChange={(e) => setQuery(e.target.value)}\n      />\n      <ClientOnly fallback={<button type=\"submit\">Search</button>}>\n        <SearchButton onSearch={() => search(query())} />\n      </ClientOnly>\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Environment-Aware Storage\n\n```tsx\nconst storage = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server((key: string) => {\n    // Server: File-based cache\n    const fs = require('node:fs')\n    return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('.cache', 'utf-8'))[key]\n  })\n  .client((key: string) => {\n    // Client: localStorage\n    return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key) || 'null')\n  })\n```\n\n## Common Problems\n\n### Environment Variable Exposure\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Exposes to client bundle\nconst apiKey = process.env.SECRET_KEY\n\n// ✅ Server-only access\nconst apiKey = createServerOnlyFn(() => process.env.SECRET_KEY)\n```\n\n### Incorrect Loader Assumptions\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Assuming loader is server-only\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users')({\n  loader: () => {\n    // This runs on BOTH server and client!\n    const secret = process.env.SECRET // Exposed to client\n    return fetch(`/api/users?key=${secret}`)\n  },\n})\n\n// ✅ Use server function for server-only operations\nconst getUsersSecurely = createServerFn().handler(() => {\n  const secret = process.env.SECRET // Server-only\n  return fetch(`/api/users?key=${secret}`)\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users')({\n  loader: () => getUsersSecurely(), // Isomorphic call to server function\n})\n```\n\n### Hydration Mismatches\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Different content server vs client\nfunction CurrentTime() {\n  return <div>{new Date().toLocaleString()}</div>\n}\n\n// ✅ Consistent rendering\nfunction CurrentTime() {\n  const [time, setTime] = createSignal<string>()\n\n  createEffect(() => {\n    setTime(new Date().toLocaleString())\n  })\n\n  return <div>{time() || 'Loading...'}</div>\n}\n```\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- [ ] **Bundle Analysis**: Verify server-only code isn't in client bundle\n- [ ] **Environment Variables**: Ensure secrets use `createServerOnlyFn()` or `createServerFn()`\n- [ ] **Loader Logic**: Remember loaders are isomorphic, not server-only\n- [ ] **ClientOnly Fallbacks**: Provide appropriate fallbacks to prevent layout shift\n- [ ] **Error Boundaries**: Handle server/client execution errors gracefully\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- [Execution Model](./execution-model.md) - Core concepts and architectural patterns\n- [Server Functions](./server-functions.md) - Deep dive into server function patterns\n- [Environment Variables](./environment-variables.md) - Secure environment variable handling\n- [Middleware](./middleware.md) - Server function middleware patterns\n"}
